intuition=[
 'Preform a passivating layer before embedding because the earlier matrix-growth route left aggregation and interfacial grain-boundary defects; this is the authors’ rationale, not a direct observation of every new film.',
 'Use slow precursor delivery to favor heterogeneous overgrowth on cores over independent ZnSe nucleation. The no-seed control supplies a qualitative comparison but no nucleation-rate constant.',
 'Exploit size-dependent poor hexane dispersibility and pyridine compatibility to purify/derivatize particles for film processing; AES supports loss of detectable phosphorus, not exact surface coverage.',
 'Separate beneficial electronic passivation from mismatch/structural defects. Enhanced UV absorption need not increase PL if thicker, defective layers increase nonradiative recombination.',
 'Distinguish shell-to-core excitation transfer in colloids from the defect-rich matrix’s inability to populate dot excitons in embedded films.',
 'Treat coordinating-solvent annealing and more coherent shells as suggested future improvements; do not insert unperformed annealing steps into the established synthesis.'
]
